{"status":"completed","summary":"Configured persistent sudo command logging on node1. Each entry includes timestamp, invoking user, target user, working directory, and command. Sudo command entries are excluded from general system logs. Configuration survived a verified node restart without changing the OS release or kernel.","actions_performed":["Added global sudo defaults using /etc/sudoers.d/command-logging.","Set /var/log/sudo-commands.log ownership to root:root and mode 0600.","Disabled sudo syslog output and disabled line wrapping.","Added weekly log rotation with 12 compressed rotations.","Validated sudoers syntax and tested logging before and after restart.","Restarted node1 once and verified recovery with a changed boot ID."],"evidence":[{"requirement":"Valid global sudo logging configuration","command_ids":["cmd-630a9d109db44451","cmd-f9addf7dc1104ca2"],"summary":"visudo parsed the configuration successfully; effective defaults show logfile=/var/log/sudo-commands.log, !syslog, and loglinelen=0."},{"requirement":"Commands include user and timestamp in the dedicated log and remain absent from general logs","command_ids":["cmd-d299ed3106444305","cmd-8b9eea4fbad04892"],"summary":"Functional probes produced timestamped root command records in the dedicated file. Matching command records in /var/log/messages and /var/log/secure totaled zero before and after restart."},{"requirement":"Installed operating-system release and kernel retained","command_ids":["cmd-58b612f386df4ea1","cmd-8b9eea4fbad04892"],"summary":"CentOS Stream 10 and kernel 6.12.0-205.el10.x86_64 were unchanged across the restart."},{"requirement":"node1 mandatory restart and recovery","command_ids":["cmd-58b612f386df4ea1","cmd-2fb4c339737e4611","cmd-8b9eea4fbad04892"],"summary":"Healthy baseline boot ID fb2aa416-d036-46d3-aeb8-30c65a01cb34 was captured, the safe reboot was acknowledged, and the recovered node reported boot ID 130f1912-52bd-4547-8580-180ea2bde7fa. Rsyslog was active, sudoers remained valid, the pre-restart record persisted, and a new post-restart sudo command was logged correctly."}]}
